stamp":1794282413519786001},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Token proof 2026-11-18 12:35 PST: read HOMEBREW_TAP_TOKEN's SSM copy (/rebar/prod/homebrew-tap-token) into a shell variable only (not printed or written; unset after), read the tap workflow state with it (`active`), and dispatched `gh workflow run autobump.yml --repo navapbc/homebrew-rebar --ref main`. Run 44392705016: event workflow_dispatch, conclusion success, log `current=0.16.0 latest=0.16.0 / already current — no-op`. Formula/rebar.rb points at nava_rebar-0.16.0.tar.gz, matching PyPI 0.16.0. Portability: the change is a GitHub Actions job on ubuntu-latest plus a YAML structure test (yaml.safe_load + string checks); no subprocesses, fds, paths, encodings or permissions in rebar code, so no Windows sweep dispatch is needed.","timestamp":1795034178769786589},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Session 05f74084 (taking over cluster B, 2026-11-18): the shared WIP was split into 3 independently reviewable Gerrit changes on current origin/main. This ticket's change is https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/3432 (release.yml homebrew_tap job + docs step 3 + test_homebrew_tap_dispatch_job). make verify on the chain tip: exit 0 (21402 + 226 passed). Note: AC1 needs Formula/rebar.rb at the latest PyPI sdist; it is at 0.16.0 = PyPI latest today (tap run 44392705016), so it is checkable now without a release.","timestamp":1795044584238295149},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Change 3432 PS1: LLM-Review +1 (4 advisories), Verified -1. The CI failure is tests/unit/test_model_classes.py::test_a_finished_gate_drive_releases_its_event_loop[raised] (run 44421131942), the flake tracked by unselfish-finnicky-whooper (added by 9ddb035cf59); this change does not touch it, and 3433, whose tree contains this change, passed Verified. Advisories addressed in PS2: the test now asserts the PyPI wait gate fails before the dispatch, and checks each `case` branch's routing separately (mutation-checked: removing the wait's `exit 1` fails it). Not changed: (a) the job does not wait for the tap run's result; recovery is documented in step 3; (b) the wait requires the version to be PyPI's latest, which holds because releases are dispatched from main only and rebar ships no prereleases (see the RC-safety note). Re-running make verify before pushing PS2.","timestamp":1795046822966088931},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Merged: change 3432 at 5532b97b1f802bcfdf114302cc78939abe9b2923 (LLM-Review +1, Verified +1 on PS2). AC evidence on origin/main 70b43262ae755785ac2e5ce1c29145a4ef244d8b, 2026-11-18 PST: `pytest tests/unit/test_release_workflow_pins.py` 32 passed (with test_release_build_check: 36); `gh api .../autobump.yml --jq .state` = active; Formula/rebar.rb url = nava_rebar-0.16.0.tar.gz and PyPI latest = 0.16.0; token dispatch run 44392705016 conclusion success (comment above); latest tap run 44430718701 (schedule) success. Unverified: the homebrew_tap job's first live run, which happens on the next release dispatch; no release was cut. Root cause: the tap bumped only on a schedule, and GitHub disables schedules after 60 days of repo inactivity, which the tap reaches between releases because it commits only on a bump.","timestamp":1795058334290949775},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Close attempt refused (no force used): the marker on the homebrew_tap step named this ticket as its sunset ticket, and src/rebar/_commands/sunset_markers.py refuses to close a ticket a tracked marker still names. The step is permanent, so I created the standing admission ticket chevrette-stony-camel (0344-6d97-3cc2-4c7b, stays open while the step exists, same pattern as cankered-cloistered-bittern) and committed e008b142ef3 repointing the marker; mechanism gate exits 0, pins tests 32 passed. make verify queued, then Gerrit.","timestamp":1795059392730448950}],"created_at":1794256240331546001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"caa7bf4e-4efb-41f2-b72e-81aaaa985a2f","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"c0a9-e8d2-8058-4250"},{"link_uuid":"9d5b0152-8f74-40c6-adc3-13b4869201f5","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"07e4-cb25-36a1-44e1"},{"link_uuid":"973562b8-ed4f-4cbf-b8ed-36f57422a937","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"db49-084c-2c0a-4039"},{"link_uuid":"23aced3b-6e5a-4740-99a3-87b17338e330","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"c98f-b7c2-6f32-4150"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\nHomebrew users of `brew install navapbc/rebar/rebar` were left 2 releases behind because the tap `navapbc/homebrew-rebar` only bumps its formula from a scheduled workflow, and GitHub disables a scheduled workflow after 60 days with no repository activity.\n\n## Observation\n- navapbc/homebrew-rebar `.github/workflows/autobump.yml` (workflow id 316476444) was in state `disabled_inactivity` (checked 2026-11-09). Its last run was a scheduled run on 2026-10-28 23:31 PDT.\n- `Formula/rebar.rb` still pointed at the nava_rebar-0.13.1 sdist, although 0.14.0 was published to PyPI on 2026-10-30. The runbook's claim that the 6-hourly schedule self-heals a missed release does not hold while the workflow is disabled.\n- GitHub disables scheduled workflows after 60 days with no repository activity. The tap only commits when a bump happens, so a gap of more than 60 days between releases disables it again.\n- Operator remediation 2026-11-09: workflow re-enabled and dispatched; on 2026-11-18 its state is `active` and `Formula/rebar.rb` points at nava_rebar-0.16.0.tar.gz, matching PyPI.\n- The tap workflow already accepts `workflow_dispatch: {}` (read from navapbc/homebrew-rebar `.github/workflows/autobump.yml` via `gh api`). The operator stored a classic `repo`-scope token as the navapbc/rebar Actions secret `HOMEBREW_TAP_TOKEN` (present in `gh api repos/navapbc/rebar/actions/secrets`) and chose the fix: rebar's release workflow triggers the tap's autobump directly.\n\n## Approach\nAdd one job, `homebrew_tap`, to `.github/workflows/release.yml`, `needs: publish` and gated on `github.event_name == 'workflow_dispatch'` like the other post-publish jobs (`github_release`, `mcp_registry`). It has `permissions: {}` because it touches only the tap, through `GH_TOKEN: ${{ secrets.HOMEBREW_TAP_TOKEN }}`, and uses no actions (so nothing new to pin). One run step:\n1. Waits (bounded, 30 x 10 s, the same shape as `mcp_registry`'s \"Wait for PyPI to serve this version\") until `https://pypi.org/pypi/nava-rebar/json` reports `info.version == inputs.version`, because the tap's script bumps only to PyPI's reported latest and would otherwise no-op on a stale CDN answer.\n2. Reads the tap workflow's state with `gh api repos/navapbc/homebrew-rebar/actions/workflows/autobump.yml --jq .state`. If it is `disabled_inactivity` it runs `gh workflow enable` (this is exactly the failure that left the tap behind); if it is `disabled_manually` it fails with an error rather than overriding a human's deliberate disable.\n3. Runs `gh workflow run autobump.yml --repo navapbc/homebrew-rebar --ref main`.\nDispatch from the release ties the bump to the release itself, so the tap no longer depends on its schedule staying alive; each bump commit also counts as tap activity. The new run step carries a `# mechanism-ok: ci_gate` marker naming this ticket, because the mechanism-delta ratchet counts every workflow run step (`scripts/_mechanism_delta/detect_ci.py` `_detect_workflow_steps`).\n\ndocs/releasing.md step 3 (\"Update the Homebrew tap\") is rewritten: the release dispatches the autobump; the schedule remains as a backstop; the inactivity-disable failure mode, how the release job handles it, and the manual recovery (`gh workflow enable` + `gh workflow run`); and the stored `HOMEBREW_TAP_TOKEN` (classic, `repo` scope, copy in SSM `/rebar/prod/homebrew-tap-token`) replacing the \"no stored cross-repo token\" claim. The \"Accounts / prerequisites\" list gains the secret.\n\n## Scope\n- `.github/workflows/release.yml` — new `homebrew_tap` job.\n- `tests/unit/test_release_workflow_pins.py` — new structural test for the job.\n- `docs/releasing.md` — step 3 and prerequisites.\n\n## Testing\n- New test `test_homebrew_tap_dispatch_job` in `tests/unit/test_release_workflow_pins.py`: the job exists, `needs` includes `publish`, `permissions` is empty, it is gated on `workflow_dispatch`, its env maps `GH_TOKEN` to `secrets.HOMEBREW_TAP_TOKEN`, and its run text contains `gh workflow run autobump.yml --repo navapbc/homebrew-rebar` and the `disabled_manually` refusal. Written first and seen failing on the unmodified workflow.\n- Failure path: the same test asserts the `disabled_manually` branch exits non-zero (the run text contains `exit 1` in that branch).\n- `make lint` (zizmor on release.yml + actionlint) and `make verify` pass.\n- Live check of the token, without cutting a release: one manual dispatch of the tap's autobump with the token read from SSM into a shell variable only (never printed or written), then the tap run's conclusion read back with `gh run list --repo navapbc/homebrew-rebar --workflow autobump.yml`. It is a no-op bump when the formula already matches PyPI.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] [non-codebase] autobump.yml is enabled and Formula/rebar.rb points at the latest PyPI sdist.\n      provenance: environment=github.com navapbc/homebrew-rebar; principal=JoeOakhartNava; privilege_posture=production-equivalent; instrument=live-call — read via gh api of the workflow state and the formula contents\n- [x] docs/releasing.md step 3 states the inactivity-disable failure mode and its recovery. Checked: reading the merged doc.\n- [x] `.github/workflows/release.yml` has a `homebrew_tap` job that runs after `publish` and dispatches navapbc/homebrew-rebar `autobump.yml` with `secrets.HOMEBREW_TAP_TOKEN`. Checked: `pytest tests/unit/test_release_workflow_pins.py` passes on merged main.\n- [x] [non-codebase] The `HOMEBREW_TAP_TOKEN` token can dispatch the tap workflow.\n      provenance: environment=github.com navapbc/homebrew-rebar; principal=HOMEBREW_TAP_TOKEN classic token (copy read from SSM /rebar/prod/homebrew-tap-token); privilege_posture=production-equivalent; instrument=live-call — one gh workflow run dispatch with the token, then the run's conclusion read back with gh run list\n","env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","file_impact":[{"path":".github/workflows/release.yml","reason":"add homebrew_tap job dispatching the tap autobump"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_release_workflow_pins.py","reason":"structural test for the homebrew_tap job"},{"path":"docs/releasing.md","reason":"step 3 describes the release-triggered dispatch, inactivity failure mode, and stored token"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","managed_refs":[["relates_to","07e4-cb25-36a1-44e1"],["relates_to","c98f-b7c2-6f32-4150"],["relates_to","db49-084c-2c0a-4039"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"792cde29-7658-48d1-8ae0-160a8ca2f25f","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"releases":[],"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"ed54-92ac-4700-43b1","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Homebrew tap autobump disabled for inactivity; formula stuck at 0.13.1, missed 0.14.0","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["7bc688f8-f2e0-4436-bab8-287d1d540237","b764d67d-eca9-4c65-8db2-c80207c99b0d","b08bfa3a-e847-48f9-9c21-b614449e6811","5973efcb-f825-4922-b89e-3542f60c5197","792cde29-7658-48d1-8ae0-160a8ca2f25f","5dad47e8-6ab5-4173-a484-c223b707230c","c10a8257-89b6-4cf1-ab19-24ef73a37eb2","1d167fb3-7719-41d7-9923-292fa4d950e0","9d5b0152-8f74-40c6-adc3-13b4869201f5","c625a069-309b-4a37-9a5a-06e281d940d3","973562b8-ed4f-4cbf-b8ed-36f57422a937","4d802c24-845a-4a16-8c66-1814f9684f2b","176e8c80-3eca-4a21-ab95-07a109eb3d14","366637e3-4c61-439f-bbee-5e5c4abbfea8","39ab3e6a-05e7-4124-9f27-4673680c34fa","23aced3b-6e5a-4740-99a3-87b17338e330"]},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1795064712953277280,"uuid":"5cb0e3d5-1dc7-49c2-9572-8d88a4e0d62d"}